+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|  MCB = Miniature Circuit Breaker                              |
|                                                               |
|  An automatically operated electrical switch that protects    |
|  low-voltage circuits from damage caused by excess current    |
|  (overload or short circuit).                                 |
|                                                               |
|  • Rated typically up to ~125 A                               |
|  • Commonly used in homes, commercial & light industrial      |
|    panels (DIN-rail mounted)                                  |
|  • Resettable (unlike fuses that must be replaced)            |
|                                                               |
|  How it works (thermal-magnetic):                             |
|  - Overload  → bimetallic strip heats & bends → trips         |
|  - Short circuit → electromagnetic coil trips almost instantly|
|                                                               |
|  Standard ratings: 6A, 10A, 16A, 20A, 25A, 32A, 40A, 63A...   |
|  Charts match these to kW loads (assuming ~230 V) to select   |
|  the right breaker for the circuit.                           |
|                                                               |
|  Purpose: Protect wiring & equipment, prevent overheating     |
|  and fire hazards. Modern replacement for many fuses.         |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
